  "query_preview": "..(Wednesday through Monday)\nIssued at 357 PM EDT MON AUG 24 2026\n\nThankfully the extended portion of the forecast seems to be fairly \ntame. The only chances for rain will come towards the beginning of \nthe forecast period starting Wednesday night, peaking on Thursday, \nand winding down again Thursday night. This will be the result of a \npassing weak cold front, which is set to move though the CWA during \nthe day Thursday. However, don't expect widespread coverage of \nprecipitation, or even a real impact on the temperature. Severe \npotential is also quite low without strong forcing, though still \ncould see some rumbles of thunder. An upper level troughing pattern \nwill be in place aloft, but our position within the trough will be \nthat of NW flow, transporting cooler and drier air aloft into the \nregion from Canada. Besides the passing cold front, the remainder of \nthe time, high pressure should dominate at the surface. The result \nwill be generally pleasant weather, with highs in the mid 80s and \nlows in the mid 60s. Things do warm up a bit towards the end of the \nperiod, with upper 80s and lower 90s currently forecast, as the \nsurface high pressure begins to shift east allowing for return \nsoutherly flow and WAA to take hold.",
